      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Melaxen treatment of bronchial asthma (BA) patients produced positive effects on biorhythms of external respiration. Quantitative characteristics of volume and speed rhythms change insignificantly. The basic quantitative effect consists in internal and external synchronization and elimination of ultradian rhythms indicating stabilization in the system of control and coordination of time structure of external respiration system."},
